  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Look at your computer keyboard. Have you ever wondered why the letters are not in "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "alphabetical",
      "ref": "v-alphabetical"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " order?"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "To answer this question, let’s "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "turn the clock back",
      "ref": "v-turn-the-clock-back"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". About 150 years ago, all letters and papers were written by hand. Things were slow and messy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Some inventors built a typing machine. The first typewriters were big and heavy. They worked like a piano."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Have you ever seen the inside of a piano? You press a key, and some "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "levers",
      "zh": "杠杆"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " will cause a "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "hammer",
      "zh": "音槌"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " to strike the correct "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "string",
      "zh": "弦"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", producing a sound. Early typewriters were similar. They had many levers. At the end of each lever, there was a letter. Press the A key, and the A lever would hit the paper and type A. The paper then moved a bit to the left. Press more keys, and you could type a word or even a book."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The first typewriters had the keys in alphabetical order. There was a problem: If you pressed two keys quickly, the levers would easily "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "jam",
      "ref": "v-jam"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "To reduce jams, people tried to "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "rearrange",
      "ref": "v-rearrange"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " the letters. American inventor Christopher Sholes invented the QWERTY keyboard. It turned out to be a great success. People around the world learnt to use the keyboard."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Many other key arrangements have since been tried. Some are "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "claimed",
      "ref": "v-claim"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " to be faster to use. However, none has been good enough to beat QWERTY. It is very difficult now to get people to change to any other key arrangement."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
